# The gate the nightly workflow (.github/workflows/nightly.yml) runs on main: coverage-not-lost on the whole suite,
# under the python3 and unittest the CI test job uses, comparing the main commit the last successful nightly ran on
# with today's. coverage.py measures every Python process a test starts, so the gate scripts the tests run are
# measured too. A report-only pilot (--soak): findings print as warnings, with the commits they came in with, and
# never fail the job, but a run that cannot be judged (exit 2) still does. Per pull request the gate runs on the
# dashboard tests only (.vibe-verifier-tests).
# --timeout: each side took 784 to 1030 seconds on ubuntu-latest (pull request #220), and the second pair runs every
# night here (the first side fills the runner's empty tool cache, so the install lines of gates/_tools.py run only at
# the base): four sides, at most 3961 seconds, plus room.
coverage-not-lost --soak --runner unittest --args "discover -s tests" --timeout 4800
